.TH GFS 1 "2026-08-12" "gfs v0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gfs \- on-demand HTTP API that creates Kubernetes Jobs for groot collect
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gfs
.br
.B gfs
.BR version | --version | -V
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gfs
is a long-lived companion to
.BR groot (1).
It stays idle until called, then creates a one-shot Kubernetes
.B Job
that runs
.B groot collect
(with optional upload configured in the Job's
.BR groot.yml ).
.PP
The process does
.B not
embed the collector. Operators deploy it in-cluster (ClusterIP) with a shared
API key. See the project
.B SPECIFICATIONS.md
for the HTTP contract, rate limits, and trusted-proxy rules.
.SH HTTP ENDPOINTS (when implemented)
.TP
.B GET /v1/collect
Minimal HTML page: API key field and button
.BR "Generate GROOT files" .
.TP
.B POST /v1/collect
Start a collect Job after API key validation. Responses include
.BR 202 ,
.BR 401 ,
.BR 409 ,
.BR 429 .
.TP
.B GET /healthz
Liveness probe (unauthenticated).
.TP
.B GET /readyz
Readiness probe (unauthenticated).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Primary settings use the
.B GROOT_TRIGGER_*
prefix (API key, log level/format, rate limits, trusted proxies) and
.B GROOT_*
keys for Job image/config (see SPECIFICATIONS.md).
.TP
.B LISTEN_ADDR
Listen address (default
.BR :8080 ).
.SH FILES
Configuration is via environment and Kubernetes objects (ConfigMap/Secret),
not a local YAML file on the trigger host.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation:
.I https://github.com/hrodrig/groot-share
.br
Collector CLI:
.BR groot (1)
(package
.BR groot ).
.SH BUGS
Report issues upstream when the GitHub repository is available.
